From: as7760 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] AS7760 test hack: SPD EEPROMs at 0x52/0x53

NOT upstreamable: retargets the T208xRDB SPD addresses for the AS7760-32X
chainload tests (two UDIMMs). Belongs in a proper AS7760 board target.

--- a/include/configs/T208xRDB.h	2026-11-14 13:06:15.677493442 -0800
+++ b/include/configs/T208xRDB.h	2026-11-14 13:06:15.862494175 -0800
@@ -74,8 +74,9 @@
 #define CFG_SYS_DDR_SDRAM_BASE	0x00000000
 #define CFG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE		CFG_SYS_DDR_SDRAM_BASE
 #define CFG_SYS_SDRAM_SIZE	2048	/* for fixed parameter use */
-#define SPD_EEPROM_ADDRESS1	0x51
-#define SPD_EEPROM_ADDRESS2	0x52
+/* AS7760-32X: two UDIMMs, SPD at 0x52/0x53 (RDB: 0x51/0x52). TEST HACK. */
+#define SPD_EEPROM_ADDRESS1	0x52
+#define SPD_EEPROM_ADDRESS2	0x53
 #define SPD_EEPROM_ADDRESS	SPD_EEPROM_ADDRESS1
 #define CTRL_INTLV_PREFERED	cacheline
